This standalone source-only collector runs the immutable original admission probe and the same Erlang source used by the SDK compiled setnode contracts in two separate fresh unnamed OTP VMs. It uses the already validated raw-byte NodeProcess capture implementation, including timeout and inherited-pipe handling. Source-build evidence, installed-root OTP_VERSION, exact probe hashes, scenario inventories, actual runtime identity and fresh output are checked; a report records raw observations without SDK expected values or a semantic compatibility claim.

The copied original admission probe observes retained external creation4, argument errors, duplicate legacy node events and kernel death/reset. The compiled driver observes missing-kernel error, inactive/active state, map monitoring, minimum active creation, already-active failure and cleanup. Its fresh scenario intentionally has no retained epoch, matching the SDK compiled fixture's creation4 case. All ETF outcomes, outer exception and raw streams remain artifacts.

